\ Bounded-memory regression for transient curry and compose products on the
\ main task.
\
\ A curry or compose result used to land its fresh instruction body on the
\ context arena, which is never reclaimed on the main task, so each of these
\ loops grew monotonically and exhausted the 4 MB cap set in the `.flags`
\ sidecar partway through. Every curry/compose product is now a refcounted
\ closure owning its body, so a dropped result is freed at the drop and both
\ loops stay flat.

20000 [ 2 [ * ] curry drop ] times
20000 [ [ 2 * ] [ 3 + ] compose drop ] times

"flat" print-line
